00:02:50.005 --> 00:02:53.005
The first, big red flag in this situation is

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:55.885
the Good Samaritan Law; a law in the U.S. specifically designed to protect

00:02:55.885 --> 00:02:58.835
people who are trying to save another person who is injured

00:02:58.835 --> 00:03:01.905
or whose life is in danger. Basically, if you're trying to help,

00:03:01.905 --> 00:03:04.915
you can't be sued later on. If you've ever taken a

00:03:04.915 --> 00:03:07.935
CPR class, one of the scenarios that they always give you is that you just

00:03:07.935 --> 00:03:10.705
come across someone who's unconscious. And you have to save them

00:03:10.705 --> 00:03:13.765
without knowing anything about them, or even whether they need

00:03:13.765 --> 00:03:16.775
saving. With Good Samaritan Laws, you know that as long as you're

00:03:16.775 --> 00:03:22.385
honestly trying to help someone in danger, you don't have to worry about injuries you might cause them, like bruising their

00:03:22.385 --> 00:03:25.235
ribs when giving them CPR, or mistaking someone who's unconscious

00:03:25.235 --> 00:03:28.195
because they're injured for someone who's just sleeping off

00:03:28.195 --> 00:03:30.775
last night's bachelor party face down in the street. Good Samaritan

00:03:30.775 --> 00:03:33.685
Laws are based off the idea that when someone potentially only

00:03:33.685 --> 00:03:36.795
has seconds to live, the last thing you want is for a bystander to

00:03:36.795 --> 00:03:39.905
hesitate or not help because it might get them in trouble. And there are

00:03:39.905 --> 00:03:42.755
plenty of examples where not having these laws in place

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.885
is really tragic. In one of the most famous examples

00:03:44.885 --> 00:03:47.065
from China, back in 2006,

00:03:47.065 --> 00:03:50.105
a man named Peng Yu encountered a woman who had fallen

00:03:50.105 --> 00:03:52.675
and broken a bone in her leg. He helped her to a hospital,

00:03:52.675 --> 00:03:55.655
but then she blamed him for her injury and then sued him!

00:03:55.655 --> 00:03:58.625
The court even ruled in her favor, leading to the infamous Peng

00:03:58.625 --> 00:04:01.645
Yu verdict, where an innocent man ended up punished for his own

00:04:01.645 --> 00:04:04.665
good deed. The outcome of this case sent a very clear message to

00:04:04.665 --> 00:04:07.655
other citizens in China: Don't help people who are in trouble.

00:04:07.655 --> 00:04:10.615
One of the scariest ways that this played out was in

00:04:10.615 --> 00:04:13.625
2011, when a toddler was the victim of a hit-and-run.

00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:16.675
A tape of the incident showed that 18 people

00:04:16.675 --> 00:04:19.165
walked past, and none stopped to help.

00:04:19.165 --> 00:04:21.960
The girl died in a hospital 8 days later. A survey

00:04:22.145 --> 00:04:25.175
